Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Little Hanuman saw a golden fruit\Nhanging in the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.02,0:00:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,He leapt for it—\Nlaughing, climbing the wind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.28,0:00:10.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Indra's thunder struck him\Nfrom the heavens.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.99,0:00:14.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The gods gathered around\Nthe fallen child.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.18,0:00:18.15,Default,,0,0,0,,They hid his strength\Nbehind a soft forgetting.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.25,0:00:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Years later, one true name\Nunlocked what sleep had sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.98,0:00:27.48,Default,,0,0,0,,What felt like weakness\Nwas only a lock.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.38,0:00:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And locks exist\Nfor the hour you are ready.
